{
  "file": "crates/habeas-sdk/tests/storage.rs",
  "item": "impl[StoredGraph/Graph]/fn[node_content]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "This storage-only consumer must delegate load/store using node_path\n without resolving contents. Graph requires the callback, but invoking\n this guard would violate the no-content-read invariant of the test.\n Other graph fixtures exercise content resolution."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/storage.rs#impl[StoredGraph/Graph]/fn[node_content]` is valid.\n\n- **Form:** It sits on an explicit function with a body. It is written as fenced citation commentary, which the built-in text accepts as a tracked justification.\n- **Substance:** The reason is not just difficulty. `StoredGraph` is a storage-only consumer. `Graph` requires `node_content`, so the method must exist. The method is deliberately a `panic!` guard, so that any content read during the storage tests fails loudly. Executing it would defeat that purpose, so zero execution is expected. The commentary also says that other graph fixtures exercise content resolution.\n- **Agreement with source:** The source matches the explanation.\n  - In `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph.rs`, `node_content` is called only from `prepare_read` and from `record_is_current` for `Dependency::Node` dependencies.\n  - The tests in `storage.rs` that use `StoredGraph` (`consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path` and `malformed_records_are_storage_errors_and_current_bad_outputs_are_output_errors`) use only `node_path`, `load_evidence`, `store_evidence`, and `StoredReview`.\n  - `StoredReview` records no content dependencies.\n  - The guard is therefore expected to stay unexecuted, as the commentary says.\n- **Scope:** The item has no other `{impl}` or `{test}` reference to `habeas:coverage`, so the citation is not redundant.\n\nI found no gap.",
